w2 free. *)\\\".\\nSyntax::sntxf: \\\"\\\" cannot be followed by \\\" point (component 3 of cell 6, = #17 of S2): it is (e1.E12).ρ(g). Read off g from the exact solutions of the orbit test (Gauss form U- D U+): a1 is fixed by the seed, a2, a3 and the torus lie in the stabilizer of [e1.E12] (so they stay free); the informative data are the upper-unipotent b's. Compare with the one-site vacuum Gauss parameters r_k(z, (w1, y)) for y = y* and the adjoint's y, and with the resolvent torus Dy[w2]. Also test the direct hypotheses H1: (e1.E12).Rrot(z,(w1,y*)).ρdiag[Dy[w2]], H2: e1.Rrot(z,(w1,y*)).ρdiag[Dy[w2]].E12 (lowering after the rotation), with y* the site-2 invariant and w2 free. *)\\\".\\nSyntax::sntxf: \\\"\\\" cannot be followed by \\\"(* the site-1 factor of the genuine [3,1,0] point (component 3 of cell 6, = #17 of S2): it is (e1.E12).ρ(g). Read off g from the exact solutions of the orbit test (Gauss form U- D U+): a1 is fixed by the seed, a2, a3 and the torus lie in the stabilizer of [e1.E12] (so they stay free); the informative data are the upper-unipotent b's. Compare with the one-site vacuum Gauss parameters r_k(z, (w1, y)) for y = y* and the adjoint's y, and with the resolvent torus Dy[w2]. Also test the direct hypotheses H1: (e1.E12).Rrot(z,(w1,y*)).ρdiag[Dy[w2]], H2: e1.Rrot(z,(w1,y*)).ρdiag[Dy[w2]].E12 (lowering after the rotation), with y* the site-2 invariant and w2 free. *)\\\".\\nSolve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\\nSolve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\\nSolve::svars: Equations may not give solutions for all \\\"solve\\\" variables.\",\n\t\"stack\": \"\"\n}",
