  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* (a, result of the previous cell) with D = rho(Dy[w2]) the undone covector g = f1.D^-1.R^-1 occupies only the weights (3,1,0), (2,2,0), (2,1,1): NO E23 component (weight (3,0,1)) and no second-order weights other than (2,1,1).  It lies in the 9-dim span e1.(words<=2) but not in the 4-dim one: the weight (2,1,1) (dim 2) carries a combination of e1.E13 and e1.E12.E23 (e1.E23.E12 = e1.E12.E23 - e1.E13 up to sign).  Minimal span: which subsets of the five covectors {e1, e1E12, e1E13, e1E12E23, e1E23E12} contain g, and the coefficients (alpha = 1) at the six w2, exact rationals. *)\nu18w = {{}, {2}, {4}, {2, 3}, {3, 2}};\nu18wn = {\"e1\", \"e1E12\", \"e1E13\", \"e1E12E23\", \"e1E23E12\"};\nu18wv = u18wordVec /@ u18w;\nu18gA[w2_] := u18g[w2, \"Dy[w2]\"];\nu18memW[w2_, sub_] := With[{B = u18wv[[sub]]}, MatrixRank[B] == Length[B] && MatrixRank[Append[B, u18gA[w2]]] == Length[B]];\nu18subsW = Subsets[Range[5], {1, 5}];\nu18memTabW = Table[{u18wn[[sub]], And @@ Table[u18memW[w2, sub], {w2, u13w2s}]}, {sub, u18subsW}];\nchecks[\"u18(a) subsets of {e1,e1E12,e1E13,e1E12E23,e1E23E12} containing g (all six w2), D = Dy[w2]\"] = Select[u18memTabW, #[[2]] &][[All, 1]];\n(* coefficients in the basis {e1, e1E12, e1E13, e1E12E23} (independent; E23E12 = E12E23 - E13 on e1, checked below) *)\nu18sub4 = {1, 2, 3, 4};\nu18coef[w2_] := Module[{s = LinearSolve[Transpose[u18wv[[u18sub4]]], u18gA[w2]]}, s/s[[1]]];\nu18coefs = Association[Table[w2 -> u18coef[w2], {w2, u13w2s}]];\nchecks[\"u18(a) e1E23E12 = e1E12E23 - e1E13 ? (rank of the three)\"] = MatrixRank[u18wv[[{3, 4, 5}]]];\nchecks[\"u18(a) coefficients (1, beta12, gamma13 [e1E13], delta [e1E12E23]) per w2\"] = u18coefs;\nGrid[Join[{{\"subset containing g (all w2)\", \"\"}}, Select[u18memTabW, #[[2]] &], {{\"w2\", \"y_A\", \"(1, beta12, gamma13, delta12.23)\"}}, Table[{w2, u14yA[w2], u18coefs[w2]}, {w2, u13w2s}]], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
