  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (2026-10-09): A1 for $[3,1,0]$ — point A is the $n=0..2$ ladder-1 $\\det_2$; its site-1 factor is a *doubly* dressed rotation; the $\\tau$'s are single Wronskians\n\nConventions: $t=\\theta_{12}$, $v_0=\\theta_1-3h$, $W(a,b)=Q^2(\\theta_1-ah)Q^3(\\theta_1-bh)-Q^3(\\theta_1-ah)Q^2(\\theta_1-bh)$ with $Q^j$ the dual $Q$'s (`QU`), $M=W(3,4)=$ `minor1`. P1 numerics, 225 states, 60 digits. (Cell 9 not run: not needed.)\n\n**(a) Dressing (cells 44–48, 61–63).** $f_{1,A}$ is **not** in span$\\{e_1^T,e_1^TE_{12},e_1^TE_{23},e_1^TE_{13}\\}\\rho(R)\\rho(D)$ for any of the 15 subsets and any $D\\in\\{\\rho(\\mathrm{Dy}[w_2]),\\rho(\\mathrm{Dy}[y_A]),1\\}$ (rank 5 vs 4 at all six $w_2$), $R=\\rho(n_A)=$ `Rrot[z,{w1,yA,w3}]` (cell 38: $v_{2,A}\\parallel e_1^T\\rho(n_A)$). With $D=\\rho(\\mathrm{Dy}[w_2])$ the undone covector $g=f_1D^{-1}R^{-1}$ occupies only the weights $(3,1,0),(2,2,0),(2,1,1)$ (no $E_{23}$ component): it lies in the 4-dim span $\\{e_1^T,\\,e_1^TE_{12},\\,e_1^TE_{13},\\,e_1^TE_{12}E_{23}\\}$ (equivalently with $e_1^TE_{23}E_{12}$ for one of the last two), in no 3-dim subset, and not in the degree-$\\le1$ span (dims of $e_1^T\\cdot$words$_{\\le k}$: 1, 4, 9, 15). Exactly\n$$f_{1,A}\\ \\propto\\ e_1^T\\big(1+\\beta E_{12}+\\gamma\\,(E_{13}+\\tfrac12E_{12}E_{23})\\big)\\,\\rho(n_A)\\,\\rho\\big((w_2-G^T)^{-1}\\big),\\qquad v_{2,A}=e_1^T\\rho(n_A),$$\n$$\\beta=\\frac{(z_1-z_2)(w_1-z_1)}{2z_2(w_1-z_2)}\\,\\frac{w_2}{w_2-z_1},\\qquad \\gamma=\\frac{(t-h)(z_1-z_3)(z_2-z_3)(w_1-z_1)}{4(t-2h)\\,z_2z_3\\,(w_1-z_3)}\\,\\frac{w_2^2}{(w_2-z_1)(y_A-z_3)},\\quad y_A=w_2\\tfrac{t-h}{t-2h}$$\n(exact rational equality at 18 $w_2$ of P1, 10 one-parameter variations of $(h,\\theta,z_k,w_1)$ and 28 random parameter points; $\\beta$ is independent of $h,\\theta,z_3$). So the dressing is a second-order element of $U(\\mathfrak n_+)$ with two parameters, the first descendant $E_{12}$ **and** the weight-$(2,1,1)$ vector $E_{13}+\\frac12E_{12}E_{23}$, plus the rotation and the resolvent torus (D = Dy[$w_2$]); no $E_{23}$ component. It is not an exponential $e^{aE_{12}+bE_{13}}$ (that would give an $E_{12}^2$ component at $(1,3,0)$).\n\n**(b) Polynomial (cells 49–53, 60).** $c_A=(0,0,-\\frac{2187}{1600},0,-\\frac{243}{80},-\\frac{27}{43},0,1,\\frac{320}{1161})$ on $(1,T_{10},T_{11},T_{20},T_{21},T_{22},T_{30},T_{31},T_{32})$, i.e. adjoint $(1,T_{10},T_{11},T_{20},T_{21})\\mapsto(T_{11},T_{21},T_{22},T_{31},T_{32})$. State independence of $f_A/$candidate (225 states): (i) $n=0..2$, $Q^{j[-]}$, minor $W(2,3)$: 22.8 (fails); **with $M=W(3,4)$: $7\\cdot10^{-48}$ (hit)**; (ii) $n=1..3$: 259 (fails); (iii) $n=0..3$ with $Q^{j[+]}$: 4.0 (fails), with $xQ^j$ and $M$: $7\\cdot10^{-48}$ (hit; same function as (i) up to a constant). Symbolic $y$: for $n=0..2$ the curve is in span$\\{1,\\tau_\\lambda\\}$ ($10^{-47}$), supported exactly on the five shapes $(1,1),(2,1),(2,2),(3,1),(3,2)$, $c(y)=(\\frac{9800}{5031}y^4,-\\frac{171500}{5031}y^3,\\frac{12005000}{216333}y^2,-\\frac{12005000}{135837}y^2,\\frac{3361400000}{17522973}y)$, and $c(y)\\parallel c_A$ **only at $y=-63/8=y_A$**; for $n=1..3$ it is in span but never parallel to $c_A$. **So point A is the ladder-1 $\\det_2$ over the adjoint pole set $n=0,1,2$** (one-site weights on $\\{0,1,2\\}$, insertion $y_A^{-(x-\\theta_1)/h}$, second column $Q^{j[-]}$), divided by the $[3,1,0]$ minor $W(3,4)$; end-to-end $\\langle\\Phi_A|\\psi\\rangle/\\langle x_0|\\psi\\rangle\\propto\\det_6/\\Psi_Q\\times\\det_2^{(0..2)}[y_A]/M$ to $5\\cdot10^{-45}$ (controls $y=-63/43,2$ fail). General form: $c_A=F(h,t,y_A)$ with $F=(2h^2(t-h)(t-2h)(t-3h)y^4,\\,2h(t-h)(t-3h)y^3,\\,(t-h)y^2,\\,(t-3h)y^2,\\,\\frac{2}{3h}y)$ on $(T_{11},T_{21},T_{22},T_{31},T_{32})$ (zero elsewhere), exact at the three numeric points of cell 12 ($h=1/2$ P1; $h=1/3$; $\\theta=(1/5,-4/9),z',w'$), and symbolically $F_kC_k=K(h,t)D_k(y)$ for all $y$ with $K=-96h^8(h-t)(2h-t)(3h-t)^2(4h-t)$, where $D$ are the coefficients of $h^4\\det_2=\\frac{y^4}4W(2,3)-\\frac{y^3}2W(1,3)+\\frac{3y^2}4W(1,2)+\\frac{y^2}4W(0,3)-\\frac y2W(0,2)$. Hence $f_A(y)=K\\,\\det_2^{(0..2)}[y]/M$ identically in $(h,t,y)$.\n\n**(c) Q-dictionary (cells 53–60).** Dual Baxter at $x$ with two dual $Q$'s ($W=W_{ij}$, pair $(2,3)$; any pair works), $\\nu_n(x)=\\prod_s(x-\\theta_s+h\\Lambda_n)$, $t_3=\\chi_3\\nu_1(x)\\nu_2(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)$:\n$$t_1(x)=\\frac{\\nu_3(x)\\,W(x{+}h,x{-}h)-\\frac{t_3(x)}{\\nu_3(x-h)\\nu_3(x-2h)}\\,W(x{-}2h,x{-}h)}{W(x,x{-}h)},\\qquad t_2(x)=\\frac{\\nu_3(x)\\nu_3(x-h)\\,W(x{+}h,x)-\\frac{t_3(x)}{\\nu_3(x-2h)}\\,W(x{-}2h,x)}{W(x,x{-}h)}.$$\nVerified on all 225 states: $\\le2\\cdot10^{-46}$ (pair (2,3)), $1.7\\cdot10^{-43}$ (pairs (1,3),(1,2)) at generic $x=3/11$, $\\theta_1-3h,\\theta_1-2h,\\theta_1-h$. Vanishing factors: at $\\theta_1-3h$ $\\nu_1(x)=0$ ($x-\\theta_1+3h$), so $t_3=0$ and only the first terms survive; none vanish at $\\theta_1-2h,\\theta_1-h$; at $x=\\theta_1$: $\\nu_3(x)=0$, $\\nu_2(x-h)=0$ so $t_3=0$, and $W_{ij}(\\theta_1,\\theta_1-h)\\equiv0$ for all pairs (i.e. $Q(\\theta_1)=\\kappa Q(\\theta_1-h)$, checked $10^{-50}$): Cramer degenerates, only $t_2(\\theta_1)=\\kappa\\,\\nu_3(\\theta_1-h)\\,t_1(\\theta_1)$ holds ($10^{-50}$), $t_1,t_2$ separately as limits ($10^{-32}$); at $\\theta_1+h$: $\\nu_3(x-h)=\\nu_3(\\theta_1)=0$ ($t_1$ drops out), $t_2(\\theta_1+h)=\\chi_3\\nu_1(\\theta_1+h)\\nu_2(\\theta_1)\\,Q^j(\\theta_1-h)/Q^j(\\theta_1)$ ($10^{-50}$, $j=1,2,3$), $t_1(\\theta_1+h)$ as a limit only.\n\nBy CBR with $W(0,1)=0$ and the Plücker relations of the $2\\times n$ matrix $(Q^2;Q^3)$, **every $\\tau_\\lambda(\\theta_1-3h)$ is a single Wronskian over the minor**:\n$$\\boxed{\\ \\tau_{(\\lambda_1,\\lambda_2)}(\\theta_1-3h)=C_\\lambda\\,\\frac{W(\\theta_1-(3-\\lambda_1)h,\\ \\theta_1-(4-\\lambda_2)h)}{W(\\theta_1-3h,\\ \\theta_1-4h)},\\quad C_\\lambda=\\prod_{k=4-\\lambda_1}^{3}kh(kh-t)\\ \\prod_{k=5-\\lambda_2}^{4}kh(kh-t)\\ }$$\n($kh(kh-t)=\\nu_3(\\theta_1-kh)$; independent of $z$ and $\\chi_3$), verified on all 225 states for the 8 nonzero shapes to $\\le3\\cdot10^{-46}$ (also against the symbolic CBR output at $P1$); $(3,3)\\mapsto W(0,1)=0$ (the vanishing operator) and $(0,0)\\mapsto1$. Ladder points needed: $\\theta_1-nh$, $n\\in\\{0..4\\}$ (from $t_a(\\theta_1-3h)$: $n=2,3,4$; $t_a(\\theta_1-2h)$: $1..4$; $t_a(\\theta_1-h)$: $0..3$; per shape: $(1,0),(1,1)$: $\\{2,3,4\\}$; $(2,1)$: $\\{1,3,4\\}$ (as single $W(1,3)/M$); the rest $\\{0..4\\}$ before simplification, but after it each is one $W(a,b)$ and $M$). In particular $\\tau_{(1,1)}=12h^2(3h-t)(4h-t)\\,W(\\theta_1-2h,\\theta_1-3h)/M$ and $\\tau_{(3,2)}=72h^5(h-t)(2h-t)(3h-t)^2(4h-t)\\,W(\\theta_1,\\theta_1-2h)/M$.\n\n**What this makes explicit.** The overlap of point A is now fully in $Q$'s: $\\langle\\Phi_A|\\Psi\\rangle=\\text{const}\\cdot\\det_6[Q_B,Q^{vac}]\\,/\\Psi_Q\\cdot\\langle x_0|\\Psi\\rangle\\cdot\\det_2^{(0..2)}[Q_B;y_A]/W(3,4)$ with $\\det_2^{(0..2)}=\\sum_{n,n'\\in\\{0,1,2\\}}w_nw_{n'}y^{n+n'}W(n,n'+1)$ — the same ladder-1 contour $\\det_2$ as for point B and the adjoint, only with the adjoint pole set $\\{0,1,2\\}$ (point B: $\\{0,..,3\\}$).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## §16. A3 (i) (spec `site1-Qform/7-undo-site2-rotation-span.md` §14): ladder-1 det2 over every pole subset P of {0,1,2,3}, |P| >= 2\n\nNew globals prefixed `u19`. Prerequisites live on K1: cells 2-7, 12, 16-21, 23, 43-63 (basisT, QU, minor1, cP3, cP2, allMats). For each of the 11 subsets: det2^{(P)}[y]/M (M = minor1 = W(3,4)) as a polynomial in the fresh symbol ySym, each y-power coefficient fitted to span{1, tau_lambda(th1-3h)} = basisT (60 digits), exact curve c^{(P)}(y), parallelism with cP3 (B) and cP2 (A), and the exact rank-1 locus of Phi(c(y)) = <Omega|(c0 + sum c_l T_l).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* det2^(P)[y] = sum_{n,m in P} w_n w_m y^(n+m) [Q2(x_n) Q3(x_m - h) - Q3(x_n) Q2(x_m - h)], x_n = th1 - n h; this is -a3 b2 + b3 a2 of the cell-18 matrix {{-<Q^j E>, <Q^j[-] E>}}, with E(x_n) = y^n. Coefficients of y^p are built directly (no symbolic Expand). *)\nu19subsets = Select[Subsets[Range[0, 3]], Length[#] >= 2 &];\nu19wg[P_, n_] := N[1/Product[(m - n) hN, {m, DeleteCases[P, n]}], precQ];\nu19q[B_, j_, n_] := QU[B, j, th1 - n hN];\nu19qm[B_, j_, n_] := QU[B, j, th1 - n hN - hN];\n(* y^p coefficient vector (225 states) of det2^(P)/minor1 *)\nu19coefs[P_] := Module[{pw = Range[0, 2 Max[P]], num, mn = Table[minor1[B], {B, nSt}]},\n  Table[Table[Sum[If[MemberQ[P, p - n], u19wg[P, n] u19wg[P, p - n] (u19q[B, 2, n] u19qm[B, 3, p - n] - u19q[B, 3, n] u19qm[B, 2, p - n]), 0], {n, P}], {B, nSt}]/mn, {p, pw}]];\n(* sanity against the cell-19 curve for P = {0..3}: coefficient vectors must equal the Expand-based fyS *)\n{u19t0, u19c0} = AbsoluteTiming[u19coefs[{0, 1, 2, 3}]];\nchecks[\"u19: direct power coefficients of det2^{0..3}/M reproduce cell-19 fyS (max abs diff)\"] = sizeQ[Max[Table[Max[Abs[u19c0[[p + 1]] - coefY[p]]], {p, 0, degY}]]];\nGrid[{{\"time (s) for one subset\", u19t0}, {\"agreement with cell 19\", checks[\"u19: direct power coefficients of det2^{0..3}/M reproduce cell-19 fyS (max abs diff)\"]}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"607004\" data-output-id=\"166\" data-out-n=\"1005\" data-sub-idx=\"10\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"66\" data-sub-start=\"11\" data-sub-end=\"11\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[1005]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"XGJlZ2lue2FycmF5fXt8Y3xjfH1caGxpbmVcdGV4dHt0aW1lIChzKSBmb3Igb25lIHN1YnNldH0gJiAwLjA5MDY3MlxcXGhsaW5lXHRleHR7YWdyZWVtZW50IHdpdGggY2VsbCAxOX0gJiA1LjI1NDI1ODUyNDMwNTMyNFx0aW1lcyAxMF57LTQ1fVxcXGhsaW5lXGVuZHthcnJheX0=\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:2.44em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.49em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.45em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">time (s) for one subset</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">agreement with cell 19</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:1.45em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0.090672</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">5.254258524305324</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">1</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">0</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8141em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mtight\">45</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:2.4em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-0.95em;\"></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-2.5em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3.7em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-4.9em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3.45em;\"></span><span class=\"hline\" style=\"border-bottom-width:0.04em;\"></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.95em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></div></div></div>",
       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
