  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (2026-10-09): A3 (i) for $[3,1,0]$ — pole-subset scan of the ladder-1 $\\det_2^{(P)}[y]/M$, $M=W(3,4)$ (cells 66–69, `u19` globals)\n\nAll **11** subsets $P\\subseteq\\{0,1,2,3\\}$, $|P|\\ge2$, give curves **in span** $\\{1,\\tau_\\lambda(\\theta_1-3h)\\}$ (max rel. residual $5\\cdot10^{-46}$, rationalization error $1.6\\cdot10^{-53}$); the curves are graded (each entry a monomial in $y$). Support (shapes with nonzero coefficient) and $y$-degree range:\n\n| P | support | y-degrees | y hits B | y hits A | rank $\\Phi(c(y))$ generic | nonzero y with $\\Phi$ rank 1 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| {0,1} | T22,T32 | 1..2 | none | none | 1 (localizing span) | all y (trivial: site-2 factor $\\Omega_1$) |\n| {0,2} | T11,T22,T31 | 2..4 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,3} | 1,T21,T30 | 3..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {1,2} | T11,T21,T22 | 2..4 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {1,3} | 1,T11,T20,T22 | 2..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {2,3} | 1,T10,T11 | 4..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,1,2} | T11,T21,T22,T31,T32 | 1..4 | none | **−63/8** | 2 | only −63/8 (= A) |\n| {0,1,3} | 1,T11,T20,T21,T22,T30,T32 | 1..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,2,3} | 1,T10,T11,T21,T22,T30,T31 | 2..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {1,2,3} | 1,T10,T11,T20,T21,T22 | 2..6 | none | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,1,2,3} | all nine | 1..6 | **−63/43** | none | 2 | only −63/43 (= B) |\n\nThe rank-1 locus is the exact common-root set of all $2\\times2$ minors of the decomposition $\\sum_kc_k(y)\\,A_k$ (cell 6's `Acoef`, polynomial gcd); y=0 is a root for every P but there $c(0)=0$ (checked), so $\\Phi=0$. **Verdict: the conjecture holds in its strong form — exactly $\\{0..3\\}\\to B$ at $y^*=-63/43$ and $\\{0,1,2\\}\\to A$ at $y_A=-63/8$, nothing else; no third point, no new continuous family.** ($P=\\{0,1\\}$ is rank 1 for all $y$ only because its support $\\{T_{22},T_{32}\\}$ lies in the localizing span.) Hence no factor identification / undo ranks were needed.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
